   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fundamental rights</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment of the Role of Ombudsman Institution; Instituional Capacity of Turkish National Police regarding Public Order Management and to Police Complaints Commission and Complaints System for the Turkish National Police(TNP), Gendarmerie and Coast Guard Increasing the Organizational Capacity of the Women and Children Sections (WCS) of the Gendarmerie General Command; Strengthening Culture of Democracy in Basic Education Institutions.AD 4b Supporting Women and Children to Eliminate the Effects of the Earthquake: The action will support women and children&#xBF;s rights in T&#xFC;rkiye through providing assistance in response to the earthquakes, which hit T&#xFC;rkiye in February 2023. Ministry of Family and Social Services and Union of Turkish Bar Associations will receive technical assistance of UN Women, UNOPS and UNICEF in order to restore and improve the services provided to women and children affected by the earthquakes</narrative>
  </description>
